// expect: a target of depth alone has one sample a pixel: a multisampled target's depth can't be read
// expect: 'target.depth' of a target with samples isn't a shader's to read (a GPU keeps several depths a pixel there), so nothing could be read of this one: leave 'samples' out, as a shadow map does, or give the target a color image, whose edges the samples smooth
// A shadow map's depth is read, which a multisampled depth can't be
scene Main { }
view Show() { var shadow = RenderTarget(64, 64, Format.Depth, samples: 4); }
